{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And the fire upon the altar.</b> The verse restored it in accordance with Rabbi Yehuda, as it is taught: Rabbi Yehuda says — from where do we derive that the kindling of the thin wood must be only on top of the altar? It is stated: <b>and the fire upon the altar</b> etc. The kindling of the thin wood — to kindle with them a large fire. אליתא — fine twigs; so it is taught, and so Rashi explained in chapter טרף בקלפי." "<b>And arrange upon it.</b> From where that he must make the large arrangement so as to receive all the burnt-offerings? It is stated: upon it. From where for the fats of sin-offering and guilt-offering and קדשי קדשים and קדשים קלים? It is stated: <b>upon it — the fats of the peace-offerings.</b> From where for the fistful and the frankincense and the meal-offering of the priests and the meal-offering of the anointed priest and the meal-offering of libations? It is stated: והקטיר, to teach concerning all burnings that they be upon it. One might think even the incense should be upon it — it is stated: ובער עליה — one burning for the incense, one arrangement for the incense."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:10:15.341119483Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}